  "raw_text": "153\n\nMana\n \n(n/s,adj)\n \n–\n \nprice, wage, value, payment, salary, expensive, costly\n \n/ precio, salario, valor, pago, caro, costoso\n\nLal mana\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfee, fine, tax\n \n/ tasa, multa, impuesto\n\nLal mana sasakra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \ntax collector\n \n/ recaudador de impuestos\n\nMamna\n \n(n/s-2p-construct)\n \n–\n \nyour wage, your salary\n \n/ tu salario\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nMamna\n \n–\n \ngroan, sigh,\nmoan, wailing\n \n/ gemido, suspiro, lamentos)\n\nMana aibapaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto pay a salary, to pay a wage, to pay a price\n \n/ pagar un salario, pagar un precio\n\n(ExEj\n(\nhf14\n):\n \nWark takram mana mai aibapi ba pamalikam lalahka baku kaiks, man silp lalahkam baku kaikpara.\n \n–\n \nView\n\nthe salary you are being paid at your work as family money, don’t view it as your own money.\n \n/ Vea el salario que le pagan\nen su trabajo como dinero familiar, no lo vea como su propio dinero.)\n\nMana luha\n \n–\n \nfree, without price, for nothing\n \n/ gratis, sin precio, por nada\n\nMana mangkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto value, to put a price on\n \n/ valorar, poner precio a\n\nMana sunaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto raise a price, to increase a price\n \n/ subir un precio, aumentar un precio\n\nMana yaia\n/yabaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto pay, to reward\n \n/ pagar, recompensar\n \n(See also\n/\n \nV\ner también:\n \nMana aibapaia\n)\n\nMana klala yabaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto give punishment to the appropriate degree, to give punishment to the\n\nappropriate amount deserved\n \n/ castigar en el grado apropiado, castigar en la cantidad adecuada\n\nmerecida\n\nKlala yabaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto give a whipping, to give a lashing, to give chastisement, to give punishment\n \n/\nazotar, castigar\n\nManakira\n \n(adj\n,\nadv)\n \n–\n \ncostly, expensive, valuable, precious, in an expensive manner\n \n/ costoso, valioso, precioso,\n\nde una manera costosa\n\nBaibil Wina Diara Manakira Ba\n \n–\n \nTreasures From God’s Word\n \n(the\n \nfirst\n \nsec\nt\nion\n \nof the mid\n-\nweek meeting)\n\n/ Tesoros de la Biblia (la primera sección de la reunión de mitad de semana)\n\nDiara manakira\n \n–\n \ntreasure, precious thing, valuable thing\n \n/ tesoro, cosa preciosa, cosa valiosa\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n05/20\n):\n \nJisas ba d\nî\na aisan kasbrika purara diara manakira suni bri ba dukiara?\n \n–\n \nWhat did Jesus say\n\nabout the storing up (of) treasure(s) in heaven?\n \n/\n \n¿Qué dijo\n \nJesús sobre de acumular tesoros en el cielo?\n)\n\nManakira kulkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto consider valuable\n \n/\n \nconsiderar valioso\n\n(ExEj\n(\nwqu\n-\n02/21\n):\n \nJehova mita waitna bara mairin ba sim sat manakira kulki ba Baibil ba nahki tanka marikisa?\n \n–\n\nHow does the Bible show\n \nthat Jehovah values men the same as women?\n \n/ ¿Cómo muestra la Biblia que Jehová\n\nvalora a los hombres por igual que a las mujeres?)\n\nWalpa manakira\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nprecious stone, precious gem\n \n/ piedra preciosa, gema preciosa\n\nSpirit dukia walpa manakira pliki\n \nsakaia\n \n–\n \nDigging for Spiritual Gems\n \n(part on Christian Life and\n\nMinistry meeting)\n \n/ Busquemos perlas escondidas (parte de la reunión\n \nVida y Ministerio\n\nCristianos)\n\nManas\n \n(also former spelling of / también la ortografía anterior de\n: Manis\n)\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nnot valuable, not costly,\nvalueless, worthless\n \n/ no valioso, no costoso, sin valor\n \nCommonly used in this way?\n\nPri sakaia mana\n \n(\ndb,wqu\n-01/24\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nransom, ransom price\n \n/ rescate, precio por el rescate\n\n(Note/Nota: Also:\n \nAtki sakan lâka\n;\n \nkm-2012-15\n \ntranslate\n \nransom\n \nas\n \nAtki sakaia lâka\n;\n \nfg\n \ntranslates\n \nransom\n \nas\n \nPri sakaia ba\n;\n\nbh\n \ntranslates as\n \nPri sakaia pura mana ba;\n \ndb-Matiu 20:28\n \ntranslates as\n \nPri sakaia mana\n;\n \ndbta-Matiu 20:28\n \ntranslates as\n\nSwaki sakanka mana\n \n/ También:\n \nAtki sakan lâka\n;\n \nkm-2012-15\n \ntraduce\n \nrescate\n \ncomo\n \nAtki sakaia lâka\n;\n \nfg\n \ntraduce\n \nrescate\n\ncomo\n \nPri sakaia ba\n;\n \nbh\n \nse traduce como\n \nPri sakaia pura mana ba\n;\n \ndb-Matiu 20:28\n \nse traduce como\n \nPri sakaia mana\n;\n\ndbta-Matiu 20:28\n \nse traduce como\n \nSwaki sakanka mana\n)\n\nSwaki sakanka mana\n \n(\ndbta-Matiu 20:28\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nransom\n \n/ rescate\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nPri sakaia mana\n)\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nkm-2012-15\n \ntranslate\n \nransom\n \nas\n \nAtki sakaia lâka\n;\n \nfg\n \ntranslates as\n \nPri sakaia ba;\n \nbh\n \ntranslates as\n \nPri sakaia\npura mana ba\n;\n \ndb-Matiu 20:28\n \ntranslates as\n \nPri sakaia mana\n \n/\n \nkm-2012-15\n \ntraduce\n \nrescate\n \ncomo\n \nAtki sakaia lâka\n;\n \nfg\n \nse\ntraduce como\n \nPri sakaia ba\n;\n \nbh\n \nse traduce como\n \nPri sakaia pura mana ba\n;\n \ndb-Matiu 20:28\n \nse traduce como\n \nPri sakaia\nmana\n)\n\nManakira\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nMana\n\nMangkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto put, to place, to deposit, to apply, to play (a video or audito recording), to sow, to plant, to assign, to\nordain, to fix into place, to arrange, to appoint\n \n/ poner, colocar, depositar, aplicar, reproducir (un video o grabación de\naudio), sembrar, plantar, asignar, ordenar, colocar, montar, concertar, nombrar\n\nAlki mangkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto get/take/catch, to put/place\n \n/ obtener, tomar, atrapar, poner, colocar\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb38\n):\n \nYawan alki silak ra mangkaia want sa\n \n–\n \nWe want to catch him and put him in jail\n \n/ Queremos atraparlo y\nmeterlo en la cárcel)\n\nAya mangkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto plant corn\n \n/ plantar maíz",
